        One obvious question is: what is programming itself?

         If you have never thought about it that way, programming is essentially the

     process of giving instructions to a computer. That is the most important idea to
 
      understand. Computers cannot truly think on their own. You might wonder, 

     “What about AI? Can’t it think?” Not really. Even AI systems mainly follow patterns
 
      and repeat processes based on the massive amounts of information they have been 
 
       trained on from the internet.
